"Returns the least-weight Hamiltonian cycle of the simple graph, or nil when there is none;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"among the optimal ones, the lexicographically least by vertex number listed from the first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex. The graph need not be complete: a missing pair is an absent edge. Tours read the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"simple graph, as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nearestNeighborTour(weight:)"},{"type":"text","text":" documents; nil below three vertices."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tour is determined for integer weights. With floating-point weights it is optimal for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sums as computed, and chosen by the same rule on them, so which of several equal tours"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"comes out, and its orientation, can depend on rounding."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The table, 2ⁿ⁻¹ · (n − 1) weights and as many validity bytes, fits in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"4 GiB: at most 25 vertices with 8-byte weights, 26 with 4-byte ones; no weight is NaN or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"infinite; the sum along any path fits in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"W"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"style":"note","type":"aside","name":"Precondition"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Θ(2ⁿ n²) time and Θ(2ⁿ n) memory: n = 20 takes 80 MB of table for 8-byte"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"weights on a complete graph, and 90 MB on another (the validity flags)."}]}],"style":"note","type":"aside","name":"Complexity"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/tours\/graphprotocols\/graph\/shortesttour(weight:)"]}],"hierarchy":